  "result": "The gate returned **OK** on its first run (9 witnesses, 19 names, no compositions), so I stopped there with 5 of the 6 runs unused.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_560_3_o1.lean`):\n- **Subject:** a vehicle (`ru_aggregate` with `DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle`).\n- **When it applies:** both of these hold:\n  - The car is in a lane or other travel region where some device requires a halt right now: railway lights flashing or a gate lowering or down, a stop sign, a red traffic signal, or a police officer or railroad flagger signalling stop.\n  - Its body is within `p.railroad_crossing_approach_reach` (15.2 m) of a railway crossing.\n- **What it requires:** there is a road edge on the highway the car is on, that edge is to the car's right (negative lateral offset), and the car's body is within `p.pullover_edge_gap` (1.0 m) of it.\n- I made no choices of my own beyond the blueprint, so I declared no narrowings.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_560_3_o1.lean`):\n- **The five planned scenarios** (`forbid`, `permit`, `idle`, `blind`, `branch_1`) are built from their narratives. In `permit` the gate is up, so the flashing lights alone trigger the halt.\n- **Four extra scenarios**, all expecting violated, cover parts of the rule the planned ones never test on their own:\n  - `branch_2`: the gate is lowering while the lights are dark.\n  - `branch_3`: a red traffic signal.\n  - `branch_4`: a police officer signalling stop.\n  - `branch_5`: the car is 0.4 m from the *left* road edge, which shows that being near an edge only counts when the edge is on the right.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
